{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"pwd; rg -n 'mechanism draws findings|Small first|preflight|One recommendation' ../../../AGENTS.md; rg -n 'pilot|Rounds 30' PAID-DESIGN.md PAID-BUILD.md; rg -n 'def (planned_days|acceptance|build_pilot|gains|bind_p|gain_credit|pair_credit|pilot_decision)' paid_run.py worksheet.py verdict.py; ls -1 paid-dry-*.log\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"pwd; rg -n 'mechanism draws findings|Small first|preflight|One recommendation' ../../../AGENTS.md; rg -n 'pilot|Rounds 30' PAID-DESIGN.md PAID-BUILD.md; rg -n 'def (planned_days|acceptance|build_pilot|gains|bind_p|gain_credit|pair_credit|pilot_decision)' paid_run.py worksheet.py verdict.py; ls -1 paid-dry-*.log\"","aggregated_output":"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window\n85:- When one mechanism draws findings round after round, stop answering findings: propose one structural rule.\n182:- Before any paid run, `python3 scripts/preflight.py` replays the stored model answers and matching records of the archives and ledgers\n354:- **Small first, then one run.** A hypothesis is first validated the simplest way, on a few stored cases and a few cents, and shown to\n357:  analysis stability test. This is a principle you should remember\"). A day or week slice before any whole-corpus run; preflight on\n363:- **One recommendation, one test.** What reaches Alex as the next step of work is one recommendation and one test of it, reached after\nPAID-DESIGN.md:204:retirement plan; its stores, archives, snapshots and summaries are kept. Its reading (`worksheet.py build-pilot`, `verdict.py --pilot`):\nPAID-DESIGN.md:206:dated summaries; the gain review when the pair is provisionally improved. The pilot's decision, by §4's precedence: a linked double\nPAID-DESIGN.md:209:\"not improved\" or \"undecided\" stops, each with its reason. The pilot never gives the comparison's pass, which needs three pairs. H3's\nPAID-DESIGN.md:210:selector and H5's duplicate counting (round 30) are fixed before the full reading, not before the pilot. Pilot cost about $1.96; the\nPAID-BUILD.md:95:## Rounds 30–31 and the pilot path\nPAID-BUILD.md:98:  estimate 18–30 reviewer-hours. Round 31 (reflection, consensus, D708): pilot first, under the rule written in PAID-DESIGN.md §8.\nPAID-BUILD.md:99:- Fixed for the pilot: the gate checks the completed calendar against the pinned one (`planned_days`, fixed apart from the replay's\nPAID-BUILD.md:103:  that date's segment range as read; `verdict.pilot_decision` reads pair 1 alone and cannot give the comparison's pass.\nPAID-BUILD.md:105:  `e2e-checks.log`: the full path's 14 checks and the pilot's 7 (a complete reading continues; never a pass; a substituted P judgement and\nPAID-BUILD.md:108:- Still open for the full reading (not the pilot): H3's selector (round 30's cases), H5's duplicate counting.\nverdict.py:41:def bind_p(rows, key, out):\nverdict.py:202:def gain_credit(gain_rows, gain_dates, segment_ends):\nverdict.py:239:def pair_credit(p_read, key, n, linked, control, gain_rows, window):\nverdict.py:247:def pilot_decision(out, p_path, h4_path, gains_path, key_path):\nworksheet.py:215:def build_pilot(out, target, key_path, seed=None):\nworksheet.py:233:def gains(out, read_sheet, key_path, target):\npaid_run.py:137:def planned_days():\npaid_run.py:362:def acceptance(summary, pinned, kind):\npaid-dry-control-1.log\npaid-dry-control-2.log\npaid-dry-control-3.log\npaid-dry-linked-1.log\npaid-dry-linked-2.log\npaid-dry-linked-3.log\npaid-dry-refused-upstream.log\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba verdict.py | sed -n '1,139p;165,335p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba verdict.py | sed -n '1,139p;165,335p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"The verdict of the paid comparison from the read worksheet and the harm findings (PAID-DESIGN.md §4), written before the run.\n     2\t\n     3\t  python3 verdict.py <out folder> <read P packet> <read H packet> <read gains packet> <key.json>      # the verdict\n     4\t  python3 verdict.py --checks                              # $0: the verdict checks, including round 25's and 26's three cases\n     5\t\n     6\tEach worksheet row carries the reader's class (definite, overlap, clear, unresolved) for a pair of answers and the dates it covers;\n     7\tdates inherit their pair's class; each arm's 73 dates are counted definite (D), not definite (N) or unresolved (U).\n     8\t`findings.json` holds `gain_reviews` {pair: {date: 'credit' | 'none' | 'unresolved' | <a class>}} covering every gain of every pair that is\n     9\tprovisionally improved (a gain: linked not definite, control definite, on that date; only gains may be adjusted), and `flags`, every one\n    10\tan explicit boolean: `h1`, `h3`, `h4_double_count`, `h5`, and the four the run summaries decide (`linked_double_refusal`,\n    11\t`infrastructure_stop`, `control_double_refusal`, `trajectory_difference`), which must agree with the six `summary.json` files.\n    12\tThe input is refused when the worksheet does not hold, for each of the six sequences, exactly one read class for each of the 73 window\n    13\tdates, when a class is not one of the four, when a flag is missing or not a boolean, when a gain review is missing or invalid, or when a\n    14\tsummary-decided flag disagrees with the summaries.\n    15\t\"\"\"\n    16\timport datetime\n    17\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    18\timport json\n    19\timport sys\n    20\t\n    21\tWINDOW_DATES = 73\n    22\tSPAN = ('2026-07-10', '2026-09-20')\n    23\tCLASSES = ('definite', 'overlap', 'clear', 'unresolved')\n    24\tFLAGS = ('linked_double_refusal', 'infrastructure_stop', 'control_double_refusal', 'trajectory_difference', 'h1', 'h3', 'h4_double_count', 'h5')\n    25\tSEQUENCES = ('linked-1', 'linked-2', 'linked-3', 'control-1', 'control-2', 'control-3')\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\tclass Refused(SystemExit):\n    29\t    pass\n    30\t\n    31\t\n    32\tdef calendar():\n    33\t    day, end = datetime.date.fromisoformat(SPAN[0]), datetime.date.fromisoformat(SPAN[1])\n    34\t    out = []\n    35\t    while day <= end:\n    36\t        out.append(day.isoformat())\n    37\t        day += datetime.timedelta(days=1)\n    38\t    return out\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\tdef bind_p(rows, key, out):\n    42\t    \"\"\"Every read P row must be a row the stores give (the same two supplying judgement ids and the same dates), and every row the stores\n    43\t    give must be read: a substituted judgement or a shifted span is refused.\"\"\"\n    44\t    import worksheet\n    45\t    expected = {}\n    46\t    for label, name in key.items():\n    47\t        for row in worksheet.p_rows(Path(out) / name, label):\n    48\t            expected[(label, row['segment judgement'], row['company judgement'])] = row['dates']\n    49\t    read = {}\n    50\t    for row in rows:\n    51\t        if row.get('part') != 'P':\n    52\t            continue\n    53\t        k = (row['sequence'], row['segment judgement'], row['company judgement'])\n    54\t        if k in read:\n    55\t            raise Refused(f'{k}: read twice')\n    56\t        read[k] = row['dates']\n    57\t    if read != expected:\n    58\t        missing, extra = set(expected) - set(read), set(read) - set(expected)\n    59\t        shifted = [k for k in set(read) & set(expected) if read[k] != expected[k]]\n    60\t        raise Refused(f'the P reading is not the stores\\' pairs: {len(missing)} missing, {len(extra)} not in the stores, {len(shifted)} with other dates')\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\tdef read_classes(rows, key, sequences=SEQUENCES):\n    64\t    \"\"\"{sequence: {date: class}}, refusing anything but exactly one valid class per window date per sequence.\"\"\"\n    65\t    window = calendar()\n    66\t    out = {name: {} for name in sequences}\n    67\t    for row in rows:\n    68\t        if row.get('part') != 'P':\n    69\t            continue\n    70\t        name = key.get(row['sequence'])\n    71\t        if name not in out:\n    72\t            raise Refused(f'unknown sequence label {row[\"sequence\"]!r}')\n    73\t        value = row['reader']['class']\n    74\t        if value not in CLASSES:\n    75\t            raise Refused(f'{row[\"sequence\"]}: class {value!r} is not one of {CLASSES}')\n    76\t        for date in row['dates']:\n    77\t            if date not in window:\n    78\t                raise Refused(f'{row[\"sequence\"]}: date {date} is outside the window')\n    79\t            if date in out[name]:\n    80\t                raise Refused(f'{row[\"sequence\"]}: date {date} read twice')\n    81\t            out[name][date] = value\n    82\t    for name, classes in out.items():\n    83\t        if sorted(classes) != window:\n    84\t            raise Refused(f'{name}: {len(classes)} dates read, not the window\\'s {len(window)}')\n    85\t    return out\n    86\t\n    87\t\n    88\tdef summary_flags(out):\n    89\t    summaries = {name: json.loads((Path(out) / name / 'summary.json').read_text()) for name in SEQUENCES}\n    90\t\n    91\t    def terminal(name):\n    92\t        return summaries[name]['terminal'].get('outcome')\n    93\t    return {'linked_double_refusal': any(terminal(n) == 'double refusal' for n in SEQUENCES if n.startswith('linked')),\n    94\t            'control_double_refusal': any(terminal(n) == 'double refusal' for n in SEQUENCES if n.startswith('control')),\n    95\t            'infrastructure_stop': any(terminal(n) == 'infrastructure stop' for n in SEQUENCES),\n    96\t            'trajectory_difference': any(not all(s['trajectory (H2)'].values()) for s in summaries.values())}\n    97\tREADABLE = 60\n    98\tCONTROL_FLOOR = 2\n    99\t\n   100\t\n   101\tdef date_classes(rows, sequence):\n   102\t    out = {}\n   103\t    for row in rows:\n   104\t        if row['sequence'] == sequence:\n   105\t            for date in row['dates']:\n   106\t                out[date] = row['reader']['class']\n   107\t    return out\n   108\t\n   109\t\n   110\tdef counts(classes, all_dates):\n   111\t    d = sum(1 for date in all_dates if classes.get(date) == 'definite')\n   112\t    u = sum(1 for date in all_dates if classes.get(date) in (None, 'unresolved'))\n   113\t    return d, u\n   114\t\n   115\t\n   116\tdef pair_outcome(linked, control, credit, all_dates):\n   117\t    \"\"\"(outcome, details): outcome is improved / not improved / undecided, or untestable / unreadable.\"\"\"\n   118\t    readable = {arm: sum(1 for date in all_dates if classes.get(date) in ('definite', 'overlap', 'clear'))\n   119\t                for arm, classes in (('linked', linked), ('control', control))}\n   120\t    adjusted = dict(linked)\n   121\t    for date, value in (credit or {}).items():\n   122\t        gain = linked.get(date) in ('overlap', 'clear') and control.get(date) == 'definite'\n   123\t        if not gain:\n   124\t            raise ValueError(f'{date}: credit may adjust only a gain (linked not definite, control definite)')\n   125\t        adjusted[date] = {'none': 'definite', 'unresolved': 'unresolved'}.get(value, value)\n   126\t    d_l, u_l = counts(adjusted, all_dates)\n   127\t    d_c, u_c = counts(control, all_dates)\n   128\t    details = {'D_L': d_l, 'U_L': u_l, 'D_C': d_c, 'U_C': u_c, 'readable': readable}\n   129\t    if min(readable.values()) < READABLE:\n   130\t        return 'unreadable', details\n   131\t    if d_c < CONTROL_FLOOR:\n   132\t        return 'untestable', details\n   133\t    if d_l + u_l < d_c:\n   134\t        return 'improved', details\n   135\t    if d_l >= d_c + u_c:\n   136\t        return 'not improved', details\n   137\t    return 'undecided', details\n   138\t\n   139\t\n   165\t    return (row['part'], row['sequence'], row['view'], row['judgement'], row.get('fixed_date'))\n   166\t\n   167\t\n   168\tdef h1(summaries):\n   169\t    \"\"\"Per pair: model refusals of readers on matched reader-days (judged in both arms), linked minus control; harm at 4 or more.\"\"\"\n   170\t    harm = {}\n   171\t    for n in ('1', '2', '3'):\n   172\t        linked, control = summaries[f'linked-{n}'], summaries[f'control-{n}']\n   173\t        days = {(j['view'], j['day']) for j in linked['reader judgements']} & {(j['view'], j['day']) for j in control['reader judgements']}\n   174\t\n   175\t        def refusals(summary):\n   176\t            return sum(1 for r in summary['archive judge rows written (dated)'] if r['reader'] and r['refused'] and (r['view'], r['day']) in days)\n   177\t        harm[n] = refusals(linked) - refusals(control) >= H1_EXCESS\n   178\t    return harm\n   179\t\n   180\t\n   181\tdef h_flags(h_rows):\n   182\t    \"\"\"H3, H4 and H5 from the read H rows.\"\"\"\n   183\t    by_key = {h_key(r): r for r in h_rows}\n   184\t    h3 = False\n   185\t    for row in h_rows:\n   186\t        if row['part'] == 'H3' and row['sequence'].startswith('linked') and row['reader']['finding'] == 'grounding error':\n   187\t            paired = row.get('paired arm in force') or {}\n   188\t            matched = [r for r in h_rows if r['part'] == 'H3' and r['sequence'] == paired.get('sequence') and r['judgement'] == paired.get('judgement')\n   189\t                       and r['reader']['finding'] == 'grounding error' and r['reader']['error type'] == row['reader']['error type']]\n   190\t            if not matched:\n   191\t                h3 = True\n   192\t    h4 = any(r['part'] == 'H4' and r['reader']['finding'] == 'double count' for r in h_rows)\n   193\t    h5 = False\n   194\t    for n in ('1', '2', '3'):\n   195\t        def failures(name):\n   196\t            return sum(1 for r in h_rows if r['part'] == 'H5' and r['sequence'] == name and r['reader']['finding'] == 'material failure')\n   197\t        if failures(f'linked-{n}') - failures(f'control-{n}') >= H5_EXCESS:\n   198\t            h5 = True\n   199\t    return {'h3': h3, 'h4_double_count': h4, 'h5': h5}, by_key\n   200\t\n   201\t\n   202\tdef gain_credit(gain_rows, gain_dates, segment_ends):\n   203\t    \"\"\"{date: adjustment} from the reviews of each gain's two supplying linked answers (rounds 29–31): a material rule-B failure must say\n   204\t    whether the reconciliation rests on it, and withdraws credit when it does ('none'); an unquantifiable CPU increment makes the date\n   205\t    unresolved (every such date marked before the pair's bounds are recomputed once); a quantified one gives the company's corrected FY2027\n   206\t    range, compared on each gain date with that date's segment range as read: definite when the segment's low end exceeds the corrected\n   207\t    high end, overlap or clear otherwise.\"\"\"\n   208\t    by_judgement = {}\n   209\t    for r in gain_rows:\n   210\t        if r['judgement'] in by_judgement:\n   211\t            raise Refused(f'gain review of judgement {r[\"judgement\"]} given twice')\n   212\t        by_judgement[r['judgement']] = r\n   213\t    credit = {}\n   214\t    for date, judgement_ids in gain_dates.items():\n   215\t        reviews = [by_judgement.get(j) for j in judgement_ids]\n   216\t        if any(r is None for r in reviews):\n   217\t            raise Refused(f'{date}: a supplying answer has no gain review')\n   218\t        for r in reviews:\n   219\t            fields = r['reader']\n   220\t            if not isinstance(fields.get('rule B material failure'), bool) or fields.get('cpu increment') not in ('none', 'quantified', 'unquantifiable'):\n   221\t                raise Refused(f'gain review of judgement {r[\"judgement\"]} is incomplete')\n   222\t            if fields['rule B material failure'] and not isinstance(fields.get('reconciliation rests on it'), bool):\n   223\t                raise Refused(f'gain review of judgement {r[\"judgement\"]}: a material failure needs a finding on reliance')\n   224\t            if fields['cpu increment'] == 'quantified' and not all(isinstance(fields.get(k), (int, float)) for k in ('corrected low', 'corrected high')):\n   225\t                raise Refused(f'gain review of judgement {r[\"judgement\"]}: a quantified CPU increment needs the corrected range')\n   226\t        if any(r['reader']['rule B material failure'] and r['reader']['reconciliation rests on it'] for r in reviews):\n   227\t            credit[date] = 'none'\n   228\t        elif any(r['reader']['cpu increment'] == 'unquantifiable' for r in reviews):\n   229\t            credit[date] = 'unresolved'\n   230\t        else:\n   231\t            corrected = [r['reader'] for r in reviews if r['reader']['cpu increment'] == 'quantified']\n   232\t            if corrected:\n   233\t                low, high = segment_ends[date]\n   234\t                c = corrected[0]\n   235\t                credit[date] = 'definite' if low > c['corrected high'] else ('clear' if high <= c['corrected low'] else 'overlap')\n   236\t    return credit\n   237\t\n   238\t\n   239\tdef pair_credit(p_read, key, n, linked, control, gain_rows, window):\n   240\t    rows = [r for r in p_read if key[r['sequence']] == f'linked-{n}']\n   241\t    supplying = {d: (r['segment judgement'], r['company judgement']) for r in rows for d in r['dates']}\n   242\t    ends = {d: (r['reader']['segment low'], r['reader']['segment high']) for r in rows for d in r['dates']}\n   243\t    gain_dates = {d: supplying[d] for d in window if linked[d] in ('overlap', 'clear') and control[d] == 'definite'}\n   244\t    return gain_credit([g for g in gain_rows if g['pair'] == n], gain_dates, ends)\n   245\t\n   246\t\n   247\tdef pilot_decision(out, p_path, h4_path, gains_path, key_path):\n   248\t    \"\"\"The pilot's decision (D708) on pair 1 alone: continue, stop (not improved, or undecided), fail (a linked double refusal) or\n   249\t    inconclusive. It never gives the comparison's pass, which needs three pairs.\"\"\"\n   250\t    import worksheet\n   251\t    summaries = {name: json.loads((Path(out) / name / 'summary.json').read_text()) for name in ('linked-1', 'control-1')}\n   252\t    if summaries['linked-1']['terminal'].get('outcome') == 'double refusal':\n   253\t        return report('fail', 'a linked double refusal')\n   254\t    if any(s['terminal'].get('outcome') != 'complete' for s in summaries.values()) or not all(s['acceptance']['accepted'] for s in summaries.values()):\n   255\t        return report('inconclusive', 'invalid or incomplete')\n   256\t    key = json.loads(Path(key_path).read_text())\n   257\t    if sorted(key.values()) != ['control-1', 'linked-1']:\n   258\t        raise Refused('the pilot key must name linked-1 and control-1')\n   259\t    p_read = json.loads(Path(p_path).read_text())\n   260\t    bind_p(p_read, key, out)\n   261\t    classes = read_classes(p_read, key, ('linked-1', 'control-1'))\n   262\t    h4 = json.loads(Path(h4_path).read_text())\n   263\t    expected = {r['judgement'] for r in worksheet.h_rows(out, 'linked-1', None) if r['part'] == 'H4'}\n   264\t    read = [r['judgement'] for r in h4 if r.get('part') == 'H4']\n   265\t    if sorted(read) != sorted(expected) or len(set(read)) != len(read):\n   266\t        raise Refused(f'the H4 reading holds {len(set(read) & expected)} of {len(expected)} post-link v14 answers (or a duplicate)')\n   267\t    if any(r['reader']['finding'] not in H_FINDINGS['H4'] for r in h4):\n   268\t        raise Refused('an H4 row has no valid finding')\n   269\t    if any(r['reader']['finding'] == 'double count' for r in h4):\n   270\t        return report('stop', 'confirmed harm (H4 double count)')\n   271\t    if h1({'linked-1': summaries['linked-1'], 'control-1': summaries['control-1'], **{f'{k}-{n}': summaries[f'{k}-1']\n   272\t                                                                                          for k in ('linked', 'control') for n in ('2', '3')}})['1']:\n   273\t        return report('stop', 'confirmed harm (H1)')\n   274\t    window = calendar()\n   275\t    linked, control = classes['linked-1'], classes['control-1']\n   276\t    provisional = pair_outcome(linked, control, {}, window)[0]\n   277\t    credit = pair_credit(p_read, key, '1', linked, control, json.loads(Path(gains_path).read_text()), window) if provisional == 'improved' else {}\n   278\t    outcome, detail = pair_outcome(linked, control, credit, window)\n   279\t    decision = {'improved': ('continue', 'pair 1 improved after the gain review, H1 and H4 clear'),\n   280\t                'not improved': ('stop', 'pair 1 not improved'), 'undecided': ('stop', 'pair 1 undecided'),\n   281\t                'untestable': ('inconclusive', 'control-1 under 2 definite dates'), 'unreadable': ('inconclusive', 'coverage short')}[outcome]\n   282\t    return report(*decision, details=dict(detail, provisional=provisional, adjusted=credit))\n   283\t\n   284\t\n   285\tdef report(outcome, reason, details=None):\n   286\t    print(json.dumps({'decision': [outcome, reason], **({'pair 1': details} if details else {})}, indent=1))\n   287\t    return outcome, reason\n   288\t\n   289\t\n   290\tdef main(out, p_path, h_path, gains_path, key_path):\n   291\t    import worksheet\n   292\t    summaries = {name: json.loads((Path(out) / name / 'summary.json').read_text()) for name in SEQUENCES}\n   293\t    flags = summary_flags(out)\n   294\t    if flags['linked_double_refusal']:                          # precedence (1), before any worksheet is required\n   295\t        print(json.dumps({'verdict': ('fail', 'a linked double refusal')}))\n   296\t        return 'fail', 'a linked double refusal'\n   297\t    if flags['infrastructure_stop'] or flags['control_double_refusal'] or flags['trajectory_difference'] or \\\n   298\t            not all(s['acceptance']['accepted'] for s in summaries.values()):\n   299\t        print(json.dumps({'verdict': ('inconclusive', 'invalid or incomplete'), 'flags': flags,\n   300\t                          'rejected': [n for n, s in summaries.items() if not s['acceptance']['accepted']]}))\n   301\t        return 'inconclusive', 'invalid or incomplete'\n   302\t    key = json.loads(Path(key_path).read_text())\n   303\t    p_read = json.loads(Path(p_path).read_text())\n   304\t    bind_p(p_read, key, out)\n   305\t    classes = read_classes(p_read, key)\n   306\t    h_rows = json.loads(Path(h_path).read_text())\n   307\t    expected = {h_key(r) for name in SEQUENCES for r in worksheet.h_rows(out, name, None)}\n   308\t    read = {h_key(r): r for r in h_rows}\n   309\t    if set(read) != expected:\n   310\t        raise Refused(f'the H packet holds {len(set(read) & expected)} of the {len(expected)} expected rows '\n   311\t                      f'({len(set(read) - expected)} unexpected)')\n   312\t    for k, row in read.items():\n   313\t        if row['reader']['finding'] not in H_FINDINGS[row['part']]:\n   314\t            raise Refused(f'{k}: finding {row[\"reader\"][\"finding\"]!r} is not one of {H_FINDINGS[row[\"part\"]]}')\n   315\t        if row['part'] == 'H3' and row['reader']['finding'] == 'grounding error' and row['reader']['error type'] not in ERROR_TYPES:\n   316\t            raise Refused(f'{k}: a grounding error needs its type, one of {ERROR_TYPES}')\n   317\t    derived, _ = h_flags(h_rows)\n   318\t    flags.update(derived)\n   319\t    flags['h1'] = any(h1(summaries).values())\n   320\t    gain_rows = json.loads(Path(gains_path).read_text())\n   321\t    window = calendar()\n   322\t    outcomes, details = [], {}\n   323\t    for n in ('1', '2', '3'):\n   324\t        linked, control = classes[f'linked-{n}'], classes[f'control-{n}']\n   325\t        provisional = pair_outcome(linked, control, {}, window)[0]\n   326\t        credit = {}\n   327\t        if provisional == 'improved':\n   328\t            credit = pair_credit(p_read, key, n, linked, control, gain_rows, window)\n   329\t        outcome, detail = pair_outcome(linked, control, credit, window)\n   330\t        outcomes.append(outcome)\n   331\t        details[n] = dict(detail, outcome=outcome, provisional=provisional, adjusted=credit)\n   332\t    result = verdict(outcomes, flags)\n   333\t    print(json.dumps({'pairs': details, 'flags': flags, 'verdict': result}, indent=1))\n   334\t    return result\n   335\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba paid_run.py | sed -n '119,159p;305,382p'; nl -ba worksheet.py | sed -n '69,98p;149,175p;211,290p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba paid_run.py | sed -n '119,159p;305,382p'; nl -ba worksheet.py | sed -n '69,98p;149,175p;211,290p'\"","aggregated_output":"   119\t\n   120\tdef pin(dry_out):\n   121\t    \"\"\"pinned-plan.json: per draw the readers and link days, the probe's job hashes, and the committed graph of the dry linked run\n   122\t    (labels included). The acceptance gate and H2 read this file, never the admission code's own tables.\"\"\"\n   123\t    pinned = {}\n   124\t    for draw in DRAWS:\n   125\t        summary = json.loads((Path(dry_out) / f'linked-{draw}' / 'summary.json').read_text())\n   126\t        pinned[draw] = {'readers': readers(draw), 'graph': summary['links committed'], 'probe jobs': sorted(window_test.probe_answers(draw))}\n   127\t    PINNED.write_text(json.dumps(pinned, indent=1))\n   128\t    print(json.dumps({d: {'readers': p['readers'], 'graph': p['graph'], 'probe jobs': len(p['probe jobs'])} for d, p in pinned.items()}, indent=1))\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\tdef pinned_plan(draw):\n   132\t    if not PINNED.exists():\n   133\t        raise SystemExit('pinned-plan.json is missing: run `pin` on the reviewed dry runs first')\n   134\t    return json.loads(PINNED.read_text())[draw]\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\tdef planned_days():\n   138\t    \"\"\"The days old-2's run completed over the window, in order: the calendar every sequence must complete.\"\"\"\n   139\t    return [r[0] for r in old2().execute('select day from days_completed where day between ? and ? order by seq', CALENDAR)]\n   140\t\n   141\t\n   142\tdef is_judgement_request(request):\n   143\t    schema = (request.get('response_format') or {}).get('json_schema') or {}\n   144\t    return schema.get('name') == 'judgement' and july_test.judged_view(request) is not None\n   145\t\n   146\t\n   147\tclass SequenceRun:\n   148\t    \"\"\"One sequence: its transport, its latch, the judging day, the upstream snapshots and the record of every judge attempt.\"\"\"\n   149\t\n   150\t    def __init__(self, kind, draw, inner, folder):\n   151\t        self.kind, self.draw, self.inner, self.folder = kind, draw, inner, folder\n   152\t        self.reader_days = readers(draw)\n   153\t        self.probe = window_test.probe_answers(draw) if kind == 'linked' else {}\n   154\t        self.stored_refusals = window_test.refused_rows()\n   155\t        self.latch = july_test.Latch()\n   156\t        self.day = None\n   157\t        self.attempts, self.refusals_given, self.link_jobs = [], [], []\n   158\t        self.snapshots, self.snapshot_problems, self.snapshot_checks = [], [], 0\n   159\t        self.day_windows, self.terminal = {}, None\n   305\t    folder = out / f'{kind}-{draw}'\n   306\t    archive, top, retired = prepare(folder, kind, draw)\n   307\t    run = SequenceRun(kind, draw, inner, folder)\n   308\t    cfg = config.load(str(V120 if kind == 'linked' else V118))\n   309\t    summary = {'kind': kind, 'draw': draw, 'transport': transport_kind, 'config': cfg.version, 'archive_top': top,\n   310\t               'reader days': run.reader_days, 'retired rows': len(retired), 'stopped': ''}\n   311\t    original_judge_day, original_build = round_module.judge_day, judging.build_prompt\n   312\t    round_module.judge_day, judging.build_prompt = run.judge_day(original_judge_day), run.build_prompt(original_build)\n   313\t    held = live_lock.acquire(str(folder / 'views.sqlite'))\n   314\t    try:\n   315\t        replay.run(testdb_path=str(ITEMS), views_path=str(folder / 'views.sqlite'), archive=archive, cfg=cfg, universe=universe.load(str(UNIVERSE)),\n   316\t                   from_day=WINDOW[0], until_day=WINDOW[1], transport=run.transport, log=lambda *a: None, only_objects={'NVDA'})\n   317\t    except Exception as error:\n   318\t        summary['stopped'] = f'{type(error).__name__}: {error}'[:500]\n   319\t        if run.terminal is None:\n   320\t            run.terminal = {'outcome': 'infrastructure stop', 'reason': summary['stopped']}\n   321\t    finally:\n   322\t        live_lock.release(held)\n   323\t        round_module.judge_day, judging.build_prompt = original_judge_day, original_build\n   324\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{folder / \"views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   325\t    reader_judgements = [dict(zip(('view', 'day', 'call_id', 'judgement_id'), r)) for r in conn.execute(\n   326\t        'select view_id, publication_day, call_id, judgement_id from judgements where view_id in (%s) order by judgement_id'\n   327\t        % ','.join('?' * len(pinned['readers'])), tuple(pinned['readers']))]\n   328\t    for j in reader_judgements:\n   329\t        window = run.day_windows.get(j['day'], (None, None))\n   330\t        j['must be fresh'] = j['day'] >= pinned['readers'][j['view']]\n   331\t        j['fresh on its day'] = window[0] is not None and window[0] < j['call_id'] <= window[1]\n   332\t        j['from the archive'] = j['call_id'] <= top\n   333\t    archive_conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{folder / \"archive.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   334\t    attempt_rows = []\n   335\t    for call_id, request_json, sha in archive_conn.execute(\"select call_id, request_json, request_sha256 from model_calls where purpose='judge' and call_id > ?\", (top,)):\n   336\t        view = july_test.judged_view(json.loads(request_json))\n   337\t        day = next((d for d, (b, a) in run.day_windows.items() if b < call_id <= a), None)\n   338\t        attempt_rows.append({'call_id': call_id, 'view': view, 'day': day, 'refused': ':refused:' in sha, 'reader': view in pinned['readers']})\n   339\t    committed = sorted(list(r) for r in conn.execute(\"select view_id, depends_on, direction, seq from dependencies where kind='reads'\"))\n   340\t    days_completed = [r[0] for r in conn.execute('select day from days_completed order by seq')]\n   341\t    with open(folder / 'snapshots.jsonl', 'w') as handle:\n   342\t        for snapshot in run.snapshots:\n   343\t            handle.write(json.dumps({'view': snapshot['view'], 'day': snapshot['day'], 'reads': snapshot['reads']}) + '\\n')\n   344\t    summary.update({\n   345\t        'terminal': run.terminal or {'outcome': 'complete'},\n   346\t        'days completed': days_completed,\n   347\t        'links committed': committed,\n   348\t        'link jobs consumed': sorted(run.link_jobs),\n   349\t        'judge attempts at the transport': run.attempts,\n   350\t        'archive judge rows written (dated)': attempt_rows,\n   351\t        'stored refusals given back': run.refusals_given,\n   352\t        'reader judgements': reader_judgements,\n   353\t        'snapshot problems': run.snapshot_problems, 'snapshot checks': run.snapshot_checks,\n   354\t        'trajectory (H2)': trajectory_check(folder / 'views.sqlite', set(pinned['readers'])),\n   355\t        'latch': run.latch.reason, 'ledger': ledger_state(),\n   356\t    })\n   357\t    summary['acceptance'] = acceptance(summary, pinned, kind)\n   358\t    (folder / 'summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   359\t    return summary\n   360\t\n   361\t\n   362\tdef acceptance(summary, pinned, kind):\n   363\t    \"\"\"The one gate for the dry runs and the paid send.\"\"\"\n   364\t    judgements = summary['reader judgements']\n   365\t    checks = {\n   366\t        'window completed, no stop': summary['stopped'] == '' and summary['terminal'] == {'outcome': 'complete'},\n   367\t        'calendar completed (every day old-2 completed)': summary.get('days completed') == planned_days(),\n   368\t        'committed graph equals the pinned one (labels included)': summary['links committed'] == (pinned['graph'] if kind == 'linked' else []),\n   369\t        'probe jobs consumed exactly the pinned set': summary['link jobs consumed'] == (pinned['probe jobs'] if kind == 'linked' else []),\n   370\t        'every post-link reader judgement fresh on its own day': all(j['fresh on its day'] for j in judgements if j['must be fresh']),\n   371\t        'every pre-link reader judgement from the archive': all(j['from the archive'] for j in judgements if not j['must be fresh']),\n   372\t        'reader judgements present': bool(judgements),\n   373\t        'upstream snapshot clean': not summary['snapshot problems'],\n   374\t        'upstream snapshot exercised (linked)': kind == 'control' or summary['snapshot checks'] > 0,\n   375\t        'fixed trajectory (H2)': all(summary['trajectory (H2)'].values()),\n   376\t        'ledger clean (not stopped, no overrun)': not (summary.get('ledger') or {}).get('stopped') and not (summary.get('ledger') or {}).get('overrun'),\n   377\t    }\n   378\t    return dict(checks, accepted=all(checks.values()))\n   379\t\n   380\t\n   381\tdef refusing_judge(label, refuse, twice=False):\n   382\t    \"\"\"July's marker judge, except that the first attempt of each (view, n) in `refuse` cites an evidence id it was not shown, so the\n    69\tdef snapshots(folder):\n    70\t    path = Path(folder) / 'snapshots.jsonl'\n    71\t    return [json.loads(line) for line in path.read_text().splitlines()] if path.exists() else []\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\tdef shown(snaps, view, day):\n    75\t    \"\"\"The read judgements a reader was shown for its judgement on `day` (the last prompt built for it that day).\"\"\"\n    76\t    built = [s for s in snaps if s['view'] == view and s['day'] == day]\n    77\t    return {target: (state or {}).get('judgement_id') for target, state in (built[-1]['reads'] if built else {}).items()}\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\tdef p_rows(folder, label):\n    81\t    conn = connect(Path(folder) / 'views.sqlite')\n    82\t    segment_rows, company_rows = judgements(conn, SEGMENT), judgements(conn, COMPANY)\n    83\t    rows = {}\n    84\t    for date in window_dates():\n    85\t        segment, company = in_force(segment_rows, date), in_force(company_rows, date)\n    86\t        if not segment or not company:\n    87\t            continue\n    88\t        key = (segment[0], company[0])\n    89\t        if key not in rows:\n    90\t            rows[key] = {'part': 'P', 'sequence': label, 'segment judgement': segment[0], 'company judgement': company[0], 'dates': [],\n    91\t                         'segment forecast': segment[2], 'segment reasons': segment[3], 'company forecast': company[2],\n    92\t                         'company reasons': company[3],\n    93\t                         'lead class': contradictions.classify(contradictions.annual(segment[2]), contradictions.annual(company[2])),\n    94\t                         'reader': dict(READER_P)}\n    95\t        rows[key]['dates'].append(date)\n    96\t    return list(rows.values())\n    97\t\n    98\t\n   149\t\n   150\tdef h_rows(out, name, label):\n   151\t    folder = Path(out) / name\n   152\t    conn, archive, snaps = connect(folder / 'views.sqlite'), connect(folder / 'archive.sqlite'), snapshots(folder)\n   153\t    reader_days = json.loads((folder / 'summary.json').read_text())['reader days']\n   154\t    pair = name.replace('linked', 'control') if name.startswith('linked') else name.replace('control', 'linked')\n   155\t    other = connect(Path(out) / pair / 'views.sqlite')\n   156\t    rows = []\n   157\t\n   158\t    def row(part, view, judgement, **extra):\n   159\t        read_ids = shown(snaps, view, judgement[1])\n   160\t        counterpart = in_force(judgements(other, view), judgement[1])\n   161\t        return {'part': part, 'sequence': name, 'view': view, 'judgement': judgement[0], 'day': judgement[1],\n   162\t                'forecast': judgement[2], 'reasons': judgement[3], 'reference': judgement[4],\n   163\t                'request': request_text(archive, judgement[5]), 'shown': read_ids, 'trace': read_judgement_trace(conn, archive, read_ids),\n   164\t                'paired arm in force': {'sequence': pair, 'judgement': counterpart[0], 'forecast': counterpart[2],\n   165\t                                        'reference': counterpart[4]} if counterpart else None,\n   166\t                **extra, 'reader': dict(READER_H)}\n   167\t    if name.startswith('linked'):\n   168\t        for j in judgements(conn, COMPANY):\n   169\t            if j[1] >= reader_days[COMPANY]:\n   170\t                rows.append(row('H4', COMPANY, j, cpu_shown=shown(snaps, COMPANY, j[1]).get(CPU)))\n   171\t    for view in (SEGMENT, COMPANY):\n   172\t        for date in FIXED_DATES:\n   173\t            j = in_force(judgements(conn, view), date)\n   174\t            if j:\n   175\t                rows.append(row('H5', view, j, fixed_date=date))\n   211\t    print(json.dumps(summary))\n   212\t    return p_packet, h_packet\n   213\t\n   214\t\n   215\tdef build_pilot(out, target, key_path, seed=None):\n   216\t    \"\"\"The pilot's packets (D708): the blind P rows of linked-1 and control-1 under two shuffled labels, and the H4 rows of linked-1 (every\n   217\t    post-link v14 answer with the CPU conclusion it saw and control-1's v14 in force); the key to <key_path>.\"\"\"\n   218\t    labels = ['S-A', 'S-B']\n   219\t    random.Random(seed).shuffle(labels) if seed is not None else random.SystemRandom().shuffle(labels)\n   220\t    key = dict(zip(labels, ('linked-1', 'control-1')))\n   221\t    p_packet = [r for label, name in key.items() for r in p_rows(Path(out) / name, label)]\n   222\t    random.Random(seed).shuffle(p_packet) if seed is not None else random.SystemRandom().shuffle(p_packet)\n   223\t    p_packet.sort(key=lambda r: ORDER.get(r['lead class'], 9))\n   224\t    h4_packet = [r for r in h_rows(out, 'linked-1', None) if r['part'] == 'H4']\n   225\t    Path(f'{target}.p.json').write_text(json.dumps(p_packet, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   226\t    Path(f'{target}.h4.json').write_text(json.dumps(h4_packet, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   227\t    Path(key_path).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   228\t    Path(key_path).write_text(json.dumps(key, indent=1))\n   229\t    print(json.dumps({'P': len(p_packet), 'H4': len(h4_packet)}))\n   230\t    return p_packet, h4_packet\n   231\t\n   232\t\n   233\tdef gains(out, read_sheet, key_path, target):\n   234\t    \"\"\"The gain review rows: for every date a linked sequence's pair is read overlap or clear while its control's is read definite, the\n   235\t    two linked answers in force (v9's and v14's), deduplicated by judgement id, each with its exact request, for rule B and H4.\"\"\"\n   236\t    key = json.loads(Path(key_path).read_text())\n   237\t    sheet = json.loads(Path(read_sheet).read_text())\n   238\t    classes = {}\n   239\t    for row in sheet:\n   240\t        if row['part'] == 'P':\n   241\t            for date in row['dates']:\n   242\t                classes[(key[row['sequence']], date)] = (row['reader']['class'], row['segment judgement'], row['company judgement'])\n   243\t    rows = []\n   244\t    for n in [p for p in ('1', '2', '3') if f'linked-{p}' in key.values()]:\n   245\t        archive = connect(Path(out) / f'linked-{n}' / 'archive.sqlite')\n   246\t        conn = connect(Path(out) / f'linked-{n}' / 'views.sqlite')\n   247\t        gain_dates = {}\n   248\t        for date in window_dates():\n   249\t            linked, control = classes.get((f'linked-{n}', date)), classes.get((f'control-{n}', date))\n   250\t            if linked and control and linked[0] in ('overlap', 'clear') and control[0] == 'definite':\n   251\t                for judgement_id in linked[1:]:\n   252\t                    gain_dates.setdefault(judgement_id, []).append(date)\n   253\t        for judgement_id, dates in sorted(gain_dates.items()):\n   254\t            j = conn.execute('select judgement_id, view_id, publication_day, implied_outcome, reasons, reference, call_id from judgements '\n   255\t                             'where judgement_id=?', (judgement_id,)).fetchone()\n   256\t            rows.append({'part': 'gain', 'pair': n, 'judgement': j[0], 'view': j[1], 'day': j[2],\n   257\t                         'forecast': j[3], 'reasons': j[4], 'reference': j[5], 'request': request_text(archive, j[6]), 'gain dates': dates,\n   258\t                         'reader': {'rule B material failure': None, 'reconciliation rests on it': None, 'cpu increment': None,\n   259\t                                    'corrected low': None, 'corrected high': None, 'note': ''}})\n   260\t    Path(target).write_text(json.dumps(rows, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   261\t    print(json.dumps({'gain review rows': len(rows)}))\n   262\t    return rows\n   263\t\n   264\t\n   265\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   266\t    if sys.argv[1] == 'build':\n   267\t        build(sys.argv[2], sys.argv[3], sys.argv[4])\n   268\t    elif sys.argv[1] == 'build-pilot':\n   269\t        build_pilot(sys.argv[2], sys.argv[3], sys.argv[4])\n   270\t    elif sys.argv[1] == 'gains':\n   271\t        gains(sys.argv[2], sys.argv[3], sys.argv[4], sys.argv[5])\n   272\t    else:\n   273\t        raise SystemExit('build or gains')\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba PAID-DESIGN.md | sed -n '73,114p;129,158p;200,230p'; nl -ba PAID-BUILD.md | sed -n '95,120p'; rg -n '\"'^## D708'\"' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba PAID-DESIGN.md | sed -n '73,114p;129,158p;200,230p'; nl -ba PAID-BUILD.md | sed -n '95,120p'; rg -n '\"'^## D708'\"' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"    73\t**Unit:** a calendar date of the fixed window 07-10..09-20 (73 dates); on each, each question's conclusion is its last accepted\n    74\tjudgement on or before the date, carried forward. A date's class comes from the **distinct answer pair** (v9's and v14's answers) in\n    75\tforce that day.\n    76\t\n    77\t**Hand classification of every distinct pair (round 23):** `contradictions.py` orders the work (definite and ambiguous first); every\n    78\tdistinct pair in all six sequences is read by hand against both answers and classed **definite** (Data Center's annual low end above\n    79\ttotal revenue's high end, as each answer finally states its FY2027 forecast), **overlap**, **clear**, or **unresolved** (an answer\n    80\tstates no FY2027 forecast that can be read). A parser class that the reading changes is recorded as a misparse with its corrected\n    81\tclass. Dates inherit their pair's class. Before reading, the pairs are listed per sequence with their date spans.\n    82\t\n    83\t**Primary line, P, per pair n (round 24: three outcomes):** over all 73 dates, each arm's dates are definite (D), not definite\n    84\t(overlap or clear, N) or unresolved (U), each date keeping its own arm's class even where the other arm is unresolved. Linked-n's\n    85\tdefinite count lies between D_L and D_L + U_L; control-n's between D_C and D_C + U_C.\n    86\t- **Improved:** D_L + U_L < D_C (the least favourable completion still has fewer definite dates in the linked arm).\n    87\t- **Not improved:** D_L >= D_C + U_C (even the most favourable completion cannot give the linked arm fewer).\n    88\t- **Undecided:** otherwise (the unresolved dates could change the result).\n    89\t- **Testable:** D_C >= 2 (known definite dates of the control over all 73, not only dates readable in both arms).\n    90\t- **Readable:** each arm has at least 60 of the 73 dates resolved **in the hand-read classes** (before any credit adjustment): a\n    91\t  coverage policy that deliberately allows at most 13 unreadable dates per arm (82.2%). A readable forecast with unsupported arithmetic\n    92\t  stays readable; its uncertainty reaches P through the credit-adjusted classes the bounds use.\n    93\t- **Credit (rounds 24–25; one rule):** a **gain** is a date on which the linked arm is not definite and the control is definite. Only\n    94\t  gains are ever adjusted; no other date's class changes for credit. When a pair is provisionally improved, **every** gain is reviewed:\n    95\t  both linked answers in force on it (v9's and v14's), deduplicated by judgement id, are read for July's rule B (arithmetic following\n    96\t  from stated inputs; each assumption that sizes the result disclosed and supported) and for H4. A gain whose forecasts carry a material\n    97\t  rule-B failure on which its reconciliation rests earns no credit (counted definite for P). A gain resting on an unsupported CPU\n    98\t  increment: when the increment can be quantified, the forecast with it removed gives the gain's credit-adjusted class; when it cannot,\n    99\t  the gain counts unresolved: **every** such gain of the pair is marked unresolved, and the bounds are then recomputed once across the\n   100\t  pair (round 26: two gains marked one at a time could each look harmless). Each date keeps its actual class in the report beside its\n   101\t  credit-adjusted class; P is recomputed on the credit-adjusted classes. A confirmed CPU double count stays a harm (H4) whatever its\n   102\t  date.\n   103\t- Reported apart, per arm: definite dates that became overlap and those that became clear.\n   104\t\n   105\t**Harm lines (each checked on all three pairs):**\n   106\t- **H1, refusals (round 24):** on **matched reader-days** (a reader judged on that day in both arms of the pair), the attempted reader\n   107\t  judgements and the model refusals among them (first attempts the code refused, terminal refusals included); refusals on linked-only\n   108\t  propagation days reported apart. Harm at **4 or more** refusals above its control on matched reader-days (3 extra is tolerated).\n   109\t  Rationale, frozen before the run: old-2's stored run refused 4 of 1,616 judgements (0.25%), about 0.6 expected per ~250 reader-days, so\n   110\t  4 extra is far above that base rate while up to 3 stays inside ordinary variation. A **linked double refusal** (the corrected answer\n   111\t  refused again: `judgement_refused_twice` stops the day) is a product failure: the verdict is **fail** whatever else holds; a control\n   112\t  double refusal makes the comparison invalid.\n   113\t- **H2, the fixed trajectory:** an unexplained difference in a non-reader request or its substantive output makes the comparison\n   114\t  **invalid** (not a harm: the paired design no longer holds).\n   129\t- **H4, the CPU link:** every post-link v14 answer in the linked sequences is read against the exact CPU conclusion it received and\n   130\t  its control's v14 answer that day. Double counting the CPU forecast is harm. Its effect on P goes only through the credit rule above.\n   131\t- **H5, arithmetic and sourcing (July's rule B):** v9 and v14 at seven fixed dates (07-12, 07-26, 08-09, 08-23, 09-06, 09-13, 09-20) in\n   132\t  all six sequences; the unit is a question-date; Claude reads first, a blind reader second; a disagreement goes to a third,\n   133\t  source-backed read whose class decides. H5 is a separate paired harm count: a linked sequence with at least 2 more material failures\n   134\t  than its control is harm. Its effect on P goes only through the credit rule above (a shared error moves no date).\n   135\t\n   136\t**Verdict precedence:** (1) a **linked double refusal** → fail; (2) **invalid or incomplete** (an infrastructure stop: budget, transport\n   137\tor harness; a control's double refusal; an H2 difference; an arm under 60 resolved dates) → inconclusive; (3) **confirmed harm** (H1, H3,\n   138\tH4 double count, H5) → fail; (4) **untestable** (a control with D_C < 2) → inconclusive, \"the class did not recur\"; (5) **P**: all three\n   139\tpairs improved → pass; any pair not improved → fail; otherwise (some pair undecided) → inconclusive.\n   140\t\n   141\t**The worksheet (pinned before the launch; rounds 24, 28, 29):** built by `worksheet.py` from the six stores and archives after the run,\n   142\tits format and code reviewed and run on the dry outputs before the send, in **two packets**: the P packet (blind: shuffled labels, no\n   143\tarm name, P rows only) for the blind reader, and the H packet (H3, H4, H5 rows, which reveal the arm through their requests); the gain\n   144\tpacket follows the P reading. `verdict.py` takes the read packets themselves: it refuses unless every expected H row (regenerated from\n   145\tthe stores) carries a valid final finding, derives H1 from the dated judge rows of the six summaries, H3–H5 from the read rows, and each\n   146\tgain's credit from the reviews of its two supplying answers; it requires all six summaries accepted by the gate, and a linked double\n   147\trefusal fails before any packet is required. One P row per distinct v9/v14 answer pair per sequence, keyed by\n   148\tboth judgement ids and the pair's date span; it carries both answers' full `implied_outcome` and reasons, and fields for the reader:\n   149\tthe FY2027 low and high ends as each answer finally states them, the excerpt they come from, the class, a note. H3, H4 and H5 rows carry\n   150\tthe exact request text (dependency block marked), the read judgement each figure came through, and the dated source quotes. Worked\n   151\texample (old-1 09-08): Data Center \"$419 billion for FY2027\" against total revenue \"$414.3 billion ... supports roughly $414–421\n   152\tbillion\": low end 419 is not above high end 421, so **overlap**, though the parser took $414.3B and flagged it definite. Claude reads\n   153\tfirst; a blind reader (Codex, labels shuffled, key kept outside the repository) second; every disagreement that could change a pair's\n   154\toutcome, an H3 or H4 finding, or an H5 mark goes to a third, source-backed read whose class decides. Reading load on old-2's schedule:\n   155\tabout 72 distinct pairs a sequence (up to 438 rows, each read twice: 876 classifications), about 213 linked v14 reviews (twice where\n   156\tan H4 finding is made), 168 H5 marks (84 question-dates twice), the H3 traces, and the full gain review (both supplying answers of every\n   157\tgain, deduplicated), before adjudication; the dry review counts each reader's rows apart; estimated 8–12 hours of reading across the\n   158\treaders, apart from the run's three hours.\n   200\t\n   201\t## 8. Staged send (D708, council round 31)\n   202\t\n   203\tPair 1 (linked-1, control-1) is registered as pair 1 of this comparison and sent first, its two arms together, on the pinned graph and\n   204\tretirement plan; its stores, archives, snapshots and summaries are kept. Its reading (`worksheet.py build-pilot`, `verdict.py --pilot`):\n   205\tthe blind P rows of both arms read by hand and bound to the stores' pairs; H4 on every post-link v14 answer of linked-1; H1 from the\n   206\tdated summaries; the gain review when the pair is provisionally improved. The pilot's decision, by §4's precedence: a linked double\n   207\trefusal fails; an invalid run, coverage short or control-1 under 2 definite dates is inconclusive; an H1 or H4 harm stops; \"improved\"\n   208\tafter the gain review continues to pairs 2 and 3 and the full reading (pair 1's remaining readings done then under the same rule);\n   209\t\"not improved\" or \"undecided\" stops, each with its reason. The pilot never gives the comparison's pass, which needs three pairs. H3's\n   210\tselector and H5's duplicate counting (round 30) are fixed before the full reading, not before the pilot. Pilot cost about $1.96; the\n   211\tceiling is Alex's (about $2.50 proposed).\n    95\t## Rounds 30–31 and the pilot path\n    96\t- Round 30 (NOT READY): H3's selector misses cases; review records not validated (a material failure without its reliance finding;\n    97\t  duplicate rows; a quantified CPU correction stored once per company judgement); completion inferred from replay returning; reading\n    98\t  estimate 18–30 reviewer-hours. Round 31 (reflection, consensus, D708): pilot first, under the rule written in PAID-DESIGN.md §8.\n    99\t- Fixed for the pilot: the gate checks the completed calendar against the pinned one (`planned_days`, fixed apart from the replay's\n   100\t  window; mutant `window cut short` caught, `paid-mutant-7.log`); `verdict.bind_p` refuses a P reading that is not exactly the stores'\n   101\t  pairs (a substituted judgement, a shifted span, a missing or duplicated row); `gain_credit` refuses a material failure without its\n   102\t  reliance finding and a duplicated review, and applies a quantified CPU correction as a corrected range compared on each gain date with\n   103\t  that date's segment range as read; `verdict.pilot_decision` reads pair 1 alone and cannot give the comparison's pass.\n   104\t- Evidence: the six dry sequences rerun with the current harness, all accepted with the calendar check (`paid-dry-*.log`);\n   105\t  `e2e-checks.log`: the full path's 14 checks and the pilot's 7 (a complete reading continues; never a pass; a substituted P judgement and\n   106\t  a missing H4 reading refused; an H4 double count stops; a quantified correction turning the gains definite stops as not improved; every\n   107\t  unquantifiable CPU gain unresolved together stops as undecided).\n   108\t- Still open for the full reading (not the pilot): H3's selector (round 30's cases), H5's duplicate counting.\n10625:## D708 · 2026-11-21 · Council R (reflection, round 31): a one-pair pilot before the full paid comparison\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba e2e_checks.py | sed -n '1,240p'; nl -ba e2e-checks.log; nl -ba paid-mutant-7.log\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba e2e_checks.py | sed -n '1,240p'; nl -ba e2e-checks.log; nl -ba paid-mutant-7.log\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"$0 end-to-end checks of the reading path on the dry stores (round 29): the worksheet packets built, a synthetic reading, and the\n     2\tverdict, then each false-pass and refusal case the review named.\n     3\t\n     4\t  python3 e2e_checks.py <dry out folder> <scratch>\n     5\t\"\"\"\n     6\timport copy\n     7\timport json\n     8\timport os\n     9\timport shutil\n    10\timport sys\n    11\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    12\t\n    13\tsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))\n    14\timport verdict                                                           # noqa: E402\n    15\timport worksheet                                                         # noqa: E402\n    16\t\n    17\t\n    18\tdef tree(out, scratch, name, edit=None):\n    19\t    \"\"\"A copy of the out folder's six sequences (stores linked, summaries copied) with `edit` applied to the summaries.\"\"\"\n    20\t    target = Path(scratch) / name\n    21\t    if target.exists():\n    22\t        shutil.rmtree(target)\n    23\t    for sequence in verdict.SEQUENCES:\n    24\t        (target / sequence).mkdir(parents=True)\n    25\t        for item in (Path(out) / sequence).iterdir():\n    26\t            if item.name != 'summary.json':\n    27\t                os.symlink(item, target / sequence / item.name)\n    28\t        summary = json.loads((Path(out) / sequence / 'summary.json').read_text())\n    29\t        if edit:\n    30\t            edit(sequence, summary)\n    31\t        (target / sequence / 'summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary))\n    32\t    return target\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\tdef read_all(packets, key, control_definite=3):\n    36\t    p, h = packets\n    37\t    p, h = copy.deepcopy(p), copy.deepcopy(h)\n    38\t    first = {}\n    39\t    for row in p:\n    40\t        first.setdefault(key[row['sequence']], []).append(row)\n    41\t    for name, rows in first.items():\n    42\t        rows.sort(key=lambda r: r['dates'][0])\n    43\t        for i, row in enumerate(rows):\n    44\t            row['reader']['class'] = 'definite' if name.startswith('control') and i < control_definite else 'clear'\n    45\t    for row in h:\n    46\t        row['reader']['finding'] = 'pass' if row['part'] == 'H5' else 'ok'\n    47\t    return p, h\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\tdef write(folder, p, h, gains):\n    51\t    for name, data in (('p.json', p), ('h.json', h), ('gains.json', gains)):\n    52\t        (Path(folder) / name).write_text(json.dumps(data))\n    53\t    return [str(Path(folder) / n) for n in ('p.json', 'h.json', 'gains.json')]\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\tdef outcome(out, files, key_path):\n    57\t    try:\n    58\t        return verdict.main(out, *files, key_path)\n    59\t    except verdict.Refused as error:\n    60\t        return ('refused', str(error)[:120])\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\tdef main(out, scratch):\n    64\t    scratch = Path(scratch)\n    65\t    scratch.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    66\t    key_path = scratch / 'key.json'\n    67\t    packets = worksheet.build(out, str(scratch / 'packet'), str(key_path), seed=7)\n    68\t    key = json.loads(key_path.read_text())\n    69\t    p, h = read_all(packets, key)\n    70\t    (scratch / 'p-read.json').write_text(json.dumps(p))\n    71\t    gains = worksheet.gains(out, str(scratch / 'p-read.json'), str(key_path), str(scratch / 'gains.json'))\n    72\t    for g in gains:\n    73\t        g['reader'].update({'rule B material failure': False, 'cpu increment': 'none'})\n    74\t    results = {}\n    75\t    files = write(scratch, p, h, gains)\n    76\t    results['a complete synthetic reading passes'] = outcome(out, files, key_path) == ('pass', 'all three pairs improved')\n    77\t    results['P rows only (no H review) is refused'] = outcome(out, write(scratch, p, [], gains), key_path)[0] == 'refused'\n    78\t    h_none = copy.deepcopy(h)\n    79\t    h_none[0]['reader']['finding'] = None\n    80\t    results['an unread H row is refused'] = outcome(out, write(scratch, p, h_none, gains), key_path)[0] == 'refused'\n    81\t    g_bad = copy.deepcopy(gains)\n    82\t    g_bad[0]['reader']['cpu increment'] = None\n    83\t    results['an incomplete gain review is refused'] = outcome(out, write(scratch, p, h, g_bad), key_path)[0] == 'refused'\n    84\t    g_fail = copy.deepcopy(gains)\n    85\t    for g in g_fail:\n    86\t        g['reader'].update({'rule B material failure': True, 'reconciliation rests on it': True})\n    87\t    results['every gain withdrawn by its reviews: not improved, fail'] = outcome(out, write(scratch, p, h, g_fail), key_path)[0] == 'fail'\n    88\t    h4 = copy.deepcopy(h)\n    89\t    next(r for r in h4 if r['part'] == 'H4')['reader']['finding'] = 'double count'\n    90\t    results['an H4 double count fails'] = outcome(out, write(scratch, p, h4, gains), key_path) == ('fail', 'confirmed harm')\n    91\t    h3 = copy.deepcopy(h)\n    92\t    row = next(r for r in h3 if r['part'] == 'H3' and r['sequence'].startswith('linked'))\n    93\t    row['reader'].update({'finding': 'grounding error', 'error type': 'own figure as market'})\n    94\t    results['a linked grounding error the control lacks fails'] = outcome(out, write(scratch, p, h3, gains), key_path) == ('fail', 'confirmed harm')\n    95\t    h5 = copy.deepcopy(h)\n    96\t    for r in [r for r in h5 if r['part'] == 'H5' and r['sequence'] == 'linked-1'][:2]:\n    97\t        r['reader']['finding'] = 'material failure'\n    98\t    results['two more H5 failures in a linked sequence fail'] = outcome(out, write(scratch, p, h5, gains), key_path) == ('fail', 'confirmed harm')\n    99\t    rejected = tree(out, scratch, 'rejected', lambda s, summary: summary['acceptance'].update(accepted=False) if s == 'control-1' else None)\n   100\t    results['a sequence the gate rejected makes it inconclusive'] = outcome(str(rejected), files, key_path)[0] == 'inconclusive'\n   101\t    double = tree(out, scratch, 'double', lambda s, summary: summary.update(terminal={'outcome': 'double refusal', 'view': 'v9'}) if s == 'linked-2' else None)\n   102\t    results['a linked double refusal fails even with no P rows'] = outcome(str(double), write(scratch, [], [], []), key_path) == ('fail', 'a linked double refusal')\n   103\t\n   104\t    files = write(scratch, p, h, gains)     # the complete reading again (the cases above overwrote the packet files)\n   105\t    control_days = {(j['view'], j['day']) for j in json.loads((Path(out) / 'control-1' / 'summary.json').read_text())['reader judgements']}\n   106\t\n   107\t    def refusals(sequence, summary):\n   108\t        if sequence == 'linked-1':          # four refusals on reader-days judged in both arms (H1 counts matched reader-days only)\n   109\t            days = [(j['view'], j['day']) for j in summary['reader judgements'] if j['must be fresh'] and (j['view'], j['day']) in control_days][:4]\n   110\t            summary['archive judge rows written (dated)'] += [{'call_id': 0, 'view': v, 'day': d, 'refused': True, 'reader': True} for v, d in days]\n   111\t    refused_tree = tree(out, scratch, 'refusals', refusals)\n   112\t    results['four more linked refusals on matched reader-days fail (H1)'] = outcome(str(refused_tree), files, key_path) == ('fail', 'confirmed harm')\n   113\t\n   114\t    def three(sequence, summary):\n   115\t        refusals(sequence, summary)\n   116\t        if sequence == 'linked-1':\n   117\t            summary['archive judge rows written (dated)'].pop()\n   118\t    results['three more are tolerated (H1)'] = outcome(str(tree(out, scratch, 'refusals-3', three)), files, key_path)[0] == 'pass'\n   119\t    g_no_reliance = copy.deepcopy(gains)\n   120\t    g_no_reliance[0]['reader']['rule B material failure'] = True\n   121\t    results['a material failure without a reliance finding is refused'] = outcome(out, write(scratch, p, h, g_no_reliance), key_path)[0] == 'refused'\n   122\t    p_sub = copy.deepcopy(p)\n   123\t    p_sub[0]['segment judgement'] += 100000\n   124\t    results['a substituted P judgement is refused'] = outcome(out, write(scratch, p_sub, h, gains), key_path)[0] == 'refused'\n   125\t    results.update(pilot_checks(out, scratch))\n   126\t    print(json.dumps(results, indent=1))\n   127\t    return all(results.values())\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\tdef pilot_checks(out, scratch):\n   131\t    \"\"\"D708's pilot path on linked-1 and control-1 of the dry stores.\"\"\"\n   132\t    folder = Path(scratch) / 'pilot'\n   133\t    folder.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   134\t    key_path = folder / 'key.json'\n   135\t    p, h4 = worksheet.build_pilot(out, str(folder / 'packet'), str(key_path), seed=3)\n   136\t    key = json.loads(key_path.read_text())\n   137\t    p, h4 = copy.deepcopy(p), copy.deepcopy(h4)\n   138\t    by = {}\n   139\t    for row in p:\n   140\t        by.setdefault(key[row['sequence']], []).append(row)\n   141\t    for name, rows in by.items():\n   142\t        rows.sort(key=lambda r: r['dates'][0])\n   143\t        for i, row in enumerate(rows):\n   144\t            definite = name == 'control-1' and i < 3\n   145\t            row['reader'].update({'class': 'definite' if definite else 'clear', 'segment low': 420.0 if definite else 380.0,\n   146\t                                  'segment high': 420.0 if definite else 380.0, 'company low': 400.0, 'company high': 400.0})\n   147\t    for row in h4:\n   148\t        row['reader']['finding'] = 'ok'\n   149\t    (folder / 'p-read.json').write_text(json.dumps(p))\n   150\t    gains = worksheet.gains(out, str(folder / 'p-read.json'), str(key_path), str(folder / 'gains.json'))\n   151\t    for g in gains:\n   152\t        g['reader'].update({'rule B material failure': False, 'cpu increment': 'none'})\n   153\t\n   154\t    def decide(p_, h4_, gains_):\n   155\t        for name, data in (('p.json', p_), ('h4.json', h4_), ('g.json', gains_)):\n   156\t            (folder / name).write_text(json.dumps(data))\n   157\t        try:\n   158\t            return verdict.pilot_decision(out, str(folder / 'p.json'), str(folder / 'h4.json'), str(folder / 'g.json'), str(key_path))\n   159\t        except verdict.Refused as error:\n   160\t            return ('refused', str(error)[:100])\n   161\t    results = {'pilot: a complete reading of an improved pair continues': decide(p, h4, gains)[0] == 'continue'}\n   162\t    results['pilot: never gives the comparison\\'s pass'] = 'pass' not in {decide(p, h4, gains)[0]}\n   163\t    sub = copy.deepcopy(p)\n   164\t    sub[0]['company judgement'] += 100000\n   165\t    results['pilot: a substituted P judgement is refused'] = decide(sub, h4, gains)[0] == 'refused'\n   166\t    results['pilot: a missing H4 reading is refused'] = decide(p, h4[1:], gains)[0] == 'refused'\n   167\t    double = copy.deepcopy(h4)\n   168\t    double[0]['reader']['finding'] = 'double count'\n   169\t    results['pilot: an H4 double count stops'] = decide(p, double, gains) == ('stop', 'confirmed harm (H4 double count)')\n   170\t    corrected = copy.deepcopy(gains)\n   171\t    for g in corrected:\n   172\t        if g['view'] == 'v14':\n   173\t            g['reader'].update({'cpu increment': 'quantified', 'corrected low': 370.0, 'corrected high': 370.0})   # below the linked segment's 380\n   174\t    results['pilot: a quantified CPU correction is applied per gain date (the gains become definite: stop)'] = \\\n   175\t        decide(p, h4, corrected) == ('stop', 'pair 1 not improved')\n   176\t    unquantified = copy.deepcopy(gains)\n   177\t    for g in unquantified:\n   178\t        if g['view'] == 'v14':\n   179\t            g['reader']['cpu increment'] = 'unquantifiable'\n   180\t    results['pilot: every unquantifiable CPU gain unresolved together (stop: undecided)'] = decide(p, h4, unquantified) == ('stop', 'pair 1 undecided')\n   181\t    return results\n   182\t\n   183\t\n   184\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   185\t    sys.exit(0 if main(sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]) else 1)\n     1\t{\"P\": 432, \"H3\": 156, \"H4\": 213, \"H5\": 84, \"H3 structural flags\": 0, \"P dates per label\": {\"S-E\": 73, \"S-A\": 73, \"S-F\": 73, \"S-D\": 73, \"S-B\": 73, \"S-C\": 73}}\n     2\t{\"gain review rows\": 18}\n     3\t{\n     4\t \"pairs\": {\n     5\t  \"1\": {\n     6\t   \"D_L\": 0,\n     7\t   \"U_L\": 0,\n     8\t   \"D_C\": 3,\n     9\t   \"U_C\": 0,\n    10\t   \"readable\": {\n    11\t    \"linked\": 73,\n    12\t    \"control\": 73\n    13\t   },\n    14\t   \"outcome\": \"improved\",\n    15\t   \"provisional\": \"improved\",\n    16\t   \"adjusted\": {}\n    17\t  },\n    18\t  \"2\": {\n    19\t   \"D_L\": 0,\n    20\t   \"U_L\": 0,\n    21\t   \"D_C\": 3,\n    22\t   \"U_C\": 0,\n    23\t   \"readable\": {\n    24\t    \"linked\": 73,\n    25\t    \"control\": 73\n    26\t   },\n    27\t   \"outcome\": \"improved\",\n    28\t   \"provisional\": \"improved\",\n    29\t   \"adjusted\": {}\n    30\t  },\n    31\t  \"3\": {\n    32\t   \"D_L\": 0,\n    33\t   \"U_L\": 0,\n    34\t   \"D_C\": 3,\n    35\t   \"U_C\": 0,\n    36\t   \"readable\": {\n    37\t    \"linked\": 73,\n    38\t    \"control\": 73\n    39\t   },\n    40\t   \"outcome\": \"improved\",\n    41\t   \"provisional\": \"improved\",\n    42\t   \"adjusted\": {}\n    43\t  }\n    44\t },\n    45\t \"flags\": {\n    46\t  \"linked_double_refusal\": false,\n    47\t  \"control_double_refusal\": false,\n    48\t  \"infrastructure_stop\": false,\n    49\t  \"trajectory_difference\": false,\n    50\t  \"h3\": false,\n    51\t  \"h4_double_count\": false,\n    52\t  \"h5\": false,\n    53\t  \"h1\": false\n    54\t },\n    55\t \"verdict\": [\n    56\t  \"pass\",\n    57\t  \"all three pairs improved\"\n    58\t ]\n    59\t}\n    60\t{\n    61\t \"