{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY.** The completed-calendar check is fixed. On the real dry stores, I still got `continue` with the forecast text, ranges, and source excerpts removed. I also got `continue` with a mismatched H4 request and with an invalid CPU correction that should have been refused. [Pilot decision](verdict.py:247) · [D708](../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10631)\n\n### Round-31 findings\n\n- **Completed calendar — fixed.** The gate compares the days recorded in the new store with old-2’s planned calendar, independent of the replay cutoff. Both pilot dry stores completed 82 days and passed. The shortened-window mutant returned normally and failed the calendar check itself. It also failed H2, so the named calendar assertion is what proves this check. [Planned days](paid_run.py:137) · [Acceptance](paid_run.py:340) · [Linked dry run](paid-dry-linked-1.log:10) · [Control dry run](paid-dry-control-1.log:10) · [Calendar mutant](paid-mutant-7.log:7)\n- **Readings bound to the stores — partly fixed.** `bind_p` checks the two judgement IDs and their exact dates. The H4 builder produced all 71 expected rows, each with the CPU snapshot and a paired control answer. But the decision checks only H4 judgement IDs and finding labels. I replaced the CPU ID and request and removed the paired control answer from one row. It still continued. P likewise accepted `clear` with a **$420B** segment and a **$400B** company, and minimal gain rows containing only IDs and verdict fields were enough to continue. [P binding](verdict.py:41) · [H4 construction](worksheet.py:150) · [H4 validation](verdict.py:262) · [Gain validation](verdict.py:202)\n- **Gain credit — partly fixed.** Missing reliance findings and duplicate gain reviews are refused. The calculation now compares the corrected company range with each date’s segment range, and unquantifiable gains are marked together. But the range check accepts `NaN`. Replacing the corrected upper bound in the dry fixture changed **stop, not improved** to **continue**. The logged correction test uses the same segment amount on every gain date, so it does not prove that one carried-forward company answer can produce different adjusted classes on different dates. [Credit calculation](verdict.py:202) · [Dry fixture](e2e_checks.py:143) · [Correction check](e2e_checks.py:170)\n\n### Required before the pilot\n\n1. **Accept reader findings against the evidence regenerated from the accepted runs.** Bind P, H4 and gain findings to their full expected rows, including the exact request and upstream and control judgements where required. Require the recorded reading fields and any required adjudication. Reject missing, substituted, duplicate or unexpected rows. The official pilot decision should require paid pair-1 summaries. The current entry point gives the same `continue` on accepted dry summaries. [Packet contract](PAID-DESIGN.md:141) · [Pilot packet builder](worksheet.py:215) · [Gain packet builder](worksheet.py:233) · [Summary and packet checks](verdict.py:247)\n2. **Validate the numbers that can change the decision.** Require finite, ordered endpoints for resolved ranges and quantified corrections. Derive the class from those ranges or refuse an inconsistent class. Add a dry case where one corrected company answer is carried across two gain dates, with one segment forecast below it and the other above it. [P rule](PAID-DESIGN.md:73) · [Class validation](verdict.py:63) · [Per-date credit](verdict.py:224)\n3. **Apply coverage before harm, as §4 prescribes.** With the linked arm below 60 resolved dates and an H4 double-count mark, I got `stop` for confirmed harm. The prescribed result is `inconclusive` for insufficient coverage. Both halt spending, but they tell Alex different things about the product. Keep linked double refusal first, then check validity and coverage, then harm, then the control floor and credited P. [Verdict precedence](PAID-DESIGN.md:136) · [Pilot branch order](verdict.py:247)\n\nH3’s selector and H5’s counting remain deferred under D708. The proposed **$2.50** ceiling still fits the **$1.96 estimated** pilot once these checks hold. [Pilot scope and ceiling](PAID-DESIGN.md:201)"}}
